        "original_id": "51606746-2317-5300-afe6-203a87e06809",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dan Balan, T.I., Rihanna, Gary Brolsma, Radu Sîrbu, Arsenie Todiraș\n- Groups: O-Zone\n- Songs and media: \"Live Your Life,\" \"Paper Trail,\" \"Dragostea Din Tei,\" \"Numa Numa\"\n- Topics: Grammy nominations, Internet memes, Moldovan music\n\nFacts:\n- O-Zone was a Moldovan pop music trio active from 1998 to 2005, and it consisted of Dan Balan, Radu Sîrbu, and Arsenie Todiraș.\n- In 2008, \"Live Your Life\" was released as a song by American rapper T.I. from his sixth studio album \"Paper Trail,\" and it featured Barbadian singer Rihanna.\n- Dan Balan was the first and only Moldovan musician to be nominated for a Grammy for co-writing Rihanna and T.I.'s \"Live Your Life.\"\n- \"Numa Numa\" is an Internet meme based on a video made by American vlogger Gary Brolsma after the song \"Dragostea Din Tei\" as performed by O-Zone.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ff4a6a7c-5bc5-547e-9fb5-976b0e3074cf",
        "text": "Page: Dan Balan. Sentence: He is the first and only Moldovan musician to be nominated for a Grammy as co-writer of Rihanna and T.I.'s \"Live Your Life\".\nPage: Live Your Life (T.I. song). Sentence: \"Live Your Life\" is a song by American rapper T.I., from his sixth studio album, \"Paper Trail\" (2008), and features Barbadian singer Rihanna.\nPage: O-Zone. Sentence: O-Zone is a Moldovan pop music trio that was active from 1998 to 2005 and consisted of Dan Balan, Radu Sîrbu, and Arsenie Todiraș.\nPage: Numa Numa (video). Sentence: Numa Numa is an Internet meme based on a video by American vlogger Gary Brolsma made after the song \"Dragostea Din Tei\" as performed by O-Zone.",
